# Panel design contract

Source of truth, in this order: the mockups in
[docs/assets/panel-redesign/panel/](docs/assets/panel-redesign/index.html),
the [components page](docs/assets/panel-redesign/panel/components.html),
`panel/outlines.json`, then
[docs/plans/panel-redesign.md](docs/plans/panel-redesign.md). Read the plan's
**The contract** and **Enforcement** sections before touching a template.

You are implementing a finished design. You are not designing.

- Build pages only from Bulma classes in the `BULMA` list of `panel/check.py`
  and from the `sp-` components on the components page, through their
  partials. No other class, no hand-written component markup, no inline style.
- No selector in `panel.css` that names a page or an id, uses `!important`, or
  sets a width outside `WIDTH_OK`. If a page looks wrong, the layout choice is
  wrong — do not patch it locally.
- If a screen seems to need a component, state or layout that does not exist:
  **stop and ask.** Do not approximate it, and do not substitute a look of
  your own.
- Never edit a mockup, `outlines.json`, `check.py`, the vendored Bulma or a
  guard test to make your work pass. A failing guard means the implementation
  is wrong. Design changes go mockup-first in a separate `design:` commit on
  the owner's explicit instruction.
- "Done" is evidence, not a description: passing `go test ./internal/web/...`
  output plus a screenshot of each restyled page from the running container,
  saved under `docs/assets/panel-redesign/evidence/` beside its mockup's name.
  Report every difference from the mockup you could not remove; do not
  describe a different result as the requested one.

After editing a fragment in `panel/src/`: `python panel/build.py`, then
`python panel/check.py` (add `--write` only when the structure change is the
point of the commit).
